WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.667
Many of Torrance's biggest constraints are set by bodies where the city shares a seat, or has none at all.

2
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:13.672
Knowing who they are, and when their decisions are still open, is one of the quickest ways to become more effective than your title suggests.

3
00:00:13.672 --> 00:00:19.438
The most time-sensitive is the Southern California Association of Governments, known as SCAG.

4
00:00:19.438 --> 00:00:24.336
It sets each city's housing target and writes the regional transportation plan.

5
00:00:24.336 --> 00:00:29.667
Torrance shares a district on SCAG's eighty-six member council with Carson and Lomita.

6
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:40.827
The method for the next housing targets is being written between now and mid 2027, with hearings in spring and summer 2027, a draft allocation in April 2028, and appeals that year.

7
00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:46.407
The time to shape Torrance's next number is during the methodology, not during the appeal.

8
00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:49.507
Los Angeles Metro decides rail and bus investment.

9
00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.615
Torrance has no seat on its board;

10
00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:56.884
it is represented by its county supervisor and a city seat held by Inglewood's mayor.

11
00:00:56.884 --> 00:01:02.836
In January 2026, Metro chose a K Line route along Hawthorne Boulevard over the city's objection.

12
00:01:02.836 --> 00:01:06.122
It is expected to open in late 2036, pending funding.

13
00:01:06.122 --> 00:01:10.356
The South Coast Air Quality Management District regulates the refinery.

14
00:01:10.356 --> 00:01:18.405
Its rule on hydrogen fluoride has been suspended since 1992, and in 2019 its board accepted voluntary safety measures instead of a ban.

15
00:01:18.405 --> 00:01:22.400
A 2026 federal bill would phase the chemical out within five years.

16
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:31.941
The county's Airport Land Use Commission reviews plans and zoning near Zamperini Field, and the council can overrule it only by a two-thirds vote with findings.

17
00:01:31.941 --> 00:01:45.357
The county's boundary commission, known as LAFCO, would decide any annexation of El Camino Village, which a city study estimated would cost twenty-seven million dollars to start and run about eleven million a year in the red.

18
00:01:45.357 --> 00:01:53.943
On the coast, Torrance has no certified local coastal program, so the Coastal Commission itself issues permits at Torrance Beach and the bluffs.

19
00:01:53.943 --> 00:02:02.649
Water comes through the Metropolitan Water District, where Torrance has its own director, and through regional groundwater and wholesale agencies.

20
00:02:02.649 --> 00:02:04.738
Transportation law has changed too.

21
00:02:04.738 --> 00:02:08.498
Under CEQA, traffic delay is no longer an environmental impact.

22
00:02:08.498 --> 00:02:10.766
The measure is vehicle miles traveled.

23
00:02:10.766 --> 00:02:23.540
Torrance's thresholds treat a project as significant if its driving per resident or employee exceeds eighty-five percent of the county average, unless it screens out as small, transit-adjacent, or fully affordable.

24
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:30.523
Delay still matters for general plan consistency and conditions, but it cannot make a project significant under CEQA.

25
00:02:30.523 --> 00:02:36.492
Separately, a 2022 law bars minimum parking requirements within half a mile of a major transit stop.

26
00:02:36.492 --> 00:02:42.341
Parts of Torrance near the transit center may already qualify, and no city map has been published.

27
00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:53.070
To influence bodies you don't sit on, work through the people who do: Torrance's SCAG representative, the South Bay Cities Council of Governments, and the county supervisor's office.

28
00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:59.319
Comment in writing while the work is still open, during methodology and rulemaking, not at final adoption.

29
00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:04.919
For more, see the regional bodies and transportation sections of the Local Official's Handbook.
